menu "Detector battery"

    config FY_BATTERY_FULL_MV
        int "Battery voltage shown as 100% (mV)"
        default 4270
        range 3500 4500
        help
            Measured battery voltage that maps to 100%. The default is what
            a Heltec V4.3 read under normal load just after a full charge was
            unplugged; it reads about 4300 mV while on the charger.

    config FY_BATTERY_EMPTY_MV
        int "Battery voltage shown as 0% (mV)"
        default 3200
        range 2800 3900
        help
            Measured battery voltage that maps to 0%. The default matches
            the protection cutoff, so the percentage is the share of runtime
            left before the board powers itself off.

    config FY_BATTERY_CUTOFF_MV
        int "Shut down below this battery voltage (mV)"
        default 3200
        range 2900 3700
        help
            Protects the cell from deep discharge. When the smoothed
            measured voltage stays below this for 30 s, the board shows a
            low-battery notice, saves open encounters, and powers off. The
            default sits past the knee of a typical single-cell Li-ion
            discharge curve and above 3.0 V even if the divider reads
            somewhat low.

    config FY_BATTERY_BOOT_MIN_MV
        int "Refuse to start below this battery voltage (mV)"
        default 3350
        range 3000 3900
        help
            Checked before anything else starts. Must be above the cutoff so
            a battery that recovers slightly at rest does not cycle the board
            on and off.

    config FY_BATTERY_RECHECK_S
        int "While off for low battery, re-check every (s)"
        default 600
        range 60 86400
        help
            A board shut down for low battery wakes briefly on this interval,
            measures without lighting the display, and starts normally once
            charging has raised the voltage above the start minimum.

endmenu
